{{!-- GM-only curation: an eye per row, toggling whether shoppers see it. Struck-through
      eye means hidden. This is the ONLY thing that takes goods off the shelf — equipped
      state is not consulted (see the note on #onShelf in merchant-sheet.js).

      dnd5e renders every section column again on each ACTIVITY row of an expanded item
      (activity.hbs, with isActivity instead of isItem), so without the isItem guard the eye
      repeated under the item, always open, and toggled the parent item. The empty cell
      stays so the grid lines up, which is what the system's own controls column does. --}}
<div class="item-detail item-shelfHide" data-column-id="shelfHide">
    {{#if isItem}}
    <button type="button" class="unbutton item-control always-interactive" data-action="toggleHidden"
            data-tooltip="{{#if ctx.shelf.hidden}}Hidden from shoppers{{else}}Visible to shoppers{{/if}}"
            aria-label="Toggle shelf visibility">
        <i class="fa-solid {{#if ctx.shelf.hidden}}fa-eye-slash{{else}}fa-eye{{/if}}" inert></i>
    </button>
    {{/if}}
</div>
